Each premarket notification submission must contain the information listed in 21 CFR 807.87:

(a) the device name, including both the trade or proprietary name and the common or usual name or classification name;
(b) the establishment registration number, if applicable, of the owner or operator submitting the notification;
(c) the class in which the device has been put under section 513 of the act and, if known, its appropriate panel; or, where the owner or operator determines the device has not been classified, a statement of that determination and its basis;
(d) action taken to comply with the performance standard requirements of section 514 of the act;
(e) proposed labels, labeling and advertisements sufficient to describe the device, its intended use and the directions for its use, with photographs or engineering drawings where applicable;
(f) a statement indicating how the device is similar to and/or different from other products of comparable type in commercial distribution, accompanied by supporting data, which may identify similar products, materials and design considerations;
(g) where the device has undergone a significant change or modification that could significantly affect safety or effectiveness, or is to be marketed for a new or different indication, the information described above on that change or modification; and
(h) a 510(k) summary as described in 807.92, or a 510(k) statement as described in 807.93.

